{title: Pouring Out My Soul}
{subtitle: 1 Samuel 1:1–28; 2:1–2}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Gm] | [Eb] |
| [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Year after year we went up to Shi[Gm]loh
[Eb]Year after year I came home [F]with empty arms
[Bb]Peninnah's children [Gm]running round the table
[Eb]And every word she said cut [F]deep and sharp
[Gm]Elkanah [F/A]asked me why [Bb]my heart was heavy
[Eb]Am I not more to you [F]than ten sons
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
With [Bb]tears I poured my prayer out [F/A]at the [Gm]doorpost of the LORD
[Eb]My lips were moving but no [F]sound came out
[Bb]Eli watched my mouth [Gm]and thought that I was drunk
No, my [Eb]lord
I am a woman in deep dis[F]tress
I have [Eb]been pouring out my soul before the [F]LORD
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Go in [Gm]peace
And may the [F/A]God of Israel grant [Eb]what you have asked of [F]him
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]My heart exults in [F/A]the [Gm]LORD
In the [Eb]LORD my horn is lifted [F]high
No one is [Bb]holy like [F/A]the [Gm]LORD
There is [Eb]none besides you
[F]And no rock like our [Bb]God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The LORD remembered me and [Gm]gave me a son
[Eb]I named him Samuel, for [F]I had asked
[Bb]I asked the LORD for him
[F/A]When he was [Gm]weaned I brought him to the temple
[Eb]To the very place I stood and [F]wept and prayed
I [Eb]prayed for this [F]child
And [Eb]the LORD has granted me what I asked of [F]him
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
My [Bb]heart exults in [F/A]the [Gm]LORD
In [Eb]the LORD my horn is lifted [F]high
No one is [Bb]holy like [F/A]the [Gm]LORD
There is [Eb]none besides you
[F]And no rock like our [Gm]God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]So now I give him to the [Bb]LORD
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
